{
  "kanji": "息",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 息\ntitle: breath\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 心\nradicalNumber: 61\nonyomi: [ソク]\nkunyomi: [いき]\ndistractors: [自, 思, 怒]\n---\n\n# 息 — breath\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 心 (no. 61) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\nThe noun [息](../words/息.md) いき means breath or breathing. In 休息 きゅうそく,\nthe character participates in a word for rest: a useful connection, but not a reason to translate every\ncompound with \"breath.\"\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** [自](自.md) sits above [心](心.md); imagine pausing to notice your own\nbreathing. This uses the modern shape, without claiming a historical derivation.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| いき | kun | [息](../words/息.md) いき — breath |\n| ソク | on | 休息 きゅうそく — rest; relaxation |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [息](../words/息.md) いき — breath; breathing\n- 休息 きゅうそく — rest\n\n## Notes\n\nThe upper part is 自, not the 田 in [思](思.md). [怒](怒.md) also has 心 below,\nbut its top is quite different. [自](自.md) alone lacks the lower heart shape.\n息 is a noun; the word article shows the verbs used to breathe in and out.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\nDictionary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1404320, 1227940.\n",
